## Tailwind

These rules add to the CSS ones and win where the two conflict; the CSS naming rules apply to the classes the project writes, not to Tailwind's utilities. Where Tailwind versions differ (CSS-first configuration with `@theme`, `@source`, and `@custom-variant`, or a `tailwind.config.js`), follow what the project uses.

### Tailwind-Formats

- Let the project's class-sorting formatter or lint rule order class lists where it has one; never hand-reorder a list it sorts.
